  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 209 AM MDT Wed Apr 22 2026\n\nWinds will weaken while remaining gusty on Friday in between\nweather systems and under fairly brisk zonal flow aloft.\nHigh temperatures will also begin to trend upward.\n\nWinds will strengthen on Saturday and Saturday night, then become\nvery strong Sunday into Sunday night, as another upper level \ntrough crossing the central Rockies steers both the polar \njetstream and subtropical jetstream over NM. A powerful shared \nenergy area between these two jetstreams has a good chance of \nproducing wind gusts over 60 mph over and just east of NM's south \ncentral mountains on Sunday and Sunday night, and potentially in \nmore locations mainly along and east of the central mountain \nchain. Humidities will again plummet mostly into the single digits\nwith a good chance for critical fire weather conditions mostly \nalong and east of the central mountain chain both Saturday and\nSunday, and potentially also in the middle and lower Rio Grande \nValley on Sunday. After high temperatures on Saturday varying from\nnear average over western areas to as much as 9 degrees above \naverage across the east, readings should fall a few to around 6 \ndegrees central and west with a Pacific cold front on Sunday. The \nupper trough will also produce a 20-50 percent chance of light \nrain showers, gusty thunderstorms, and high terrain snow showers \nalong and west of the northern mountains Saturday through Sunday. \n\nExcept for some cooling behind a backdoor cold front that sags \ninto the eastern plains Sunday night into Monday, temperatures\nwill trend warmer early in the coming work week as a modest ridge\nof high pressure crosses. Winds will still be seasonably gusty on\nMonday, then they look to become strong again on Tuesday as \nspeeds aloft strengthen again on the back side of the ridge and a \nsharp lee-side surface trough redevelops. By Tuesday, high\ntemperatures should vary from near to as much as 10 degrees above\naverage.",
